\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Davis sat stoically and silently through the trial's first week in front of the jury, a contrast to the recordings they were watching of him going on for literally hours about his criminal history.}{\rtlch\afs24
\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2
\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 But by Friday, and with jurors barely out of the room for a recess, Keffe D couldn't hold his tongue any longer, accusing the prosecutor's office and their witnesses of putting his address on the street.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24
\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2 "They broke in my house, vandalized my house, vandalized my wife's car, you know what I'm saying?" he told Kierny. "Because they keep giving out my address. Now they gave out my sister's address. This stuff is wrong."}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}
